# Why Does This Work?

Every valid trade removes exactly one surrounded block of ones.

Removing that block joins the left and right zero runs into one larger zero run.

The size of the removable one block gets added to the merged zero block but is also removed from the existing ones count, so it cancels out.

Therefore, the only extra active sections gained are:

```
left zero run
+
right zero run
```

So we only need the lengths of consecutive zero runs.

